.TH RICK_CLOCK_TEST 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
rick_clock_test \- reprogram the DTC timing-card oscillator to 200 MHz (development test)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rick_clock_test
.RB [ \-h | \-V | \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens
.BI /dev/mu2e N
(N from
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
else 0) read-only and, unconditionally, performs the IIC write sequence through
registers 0x9168/0x916C that freezes the DCO of the oscillator at IIC address
0x5D, writes new HS_DIV/N1/RFREQ values for 200 MHz, unfreezes it and sets
NewFreq.
After each write it polls 0x916C until it reads other than 1, with no timeout.
.PP
The usage text (start, stop, dump, read, write, write_loopback_data) is stale:
command arguments are ignored and every invocation other than
.BR \-h ,
.BR \-?
and
.B \-V
reprograms the clock.
.B \-d
appears in the source but not in the getopt string, so it is rejected
(usage, exit 0).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-?
Usage, exit 0.
.TP
.B \-V
RCS revision, exit 0.
.TP
.B \-v
Accepted, no effect.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 after the sequence (prints
.BR sts=0 );
1 if the open or any ioctl fails.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B DTCLIB_DTC
selects the card.
.SH WARNINGS
Destructive: changes the clock of a live card with no confirmation.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
DTCLIB_DTC=2 rick_clock_test
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR my_cntl (1),
.BR mu2eUtil (1),
.BR mu2e (4)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
